! Exclusions (ordered, first match wins; leading ! means keep).
! This testmod runs the gasaerexch+rename head of the cluster off the unified
! multi-snapshot pair: ncdata = the before tape (working vmr and the setsox
! "other" tendency read at P_start, the post-setsox / gasaerexch entry);
! ncdata_check = the after tape, whose plain aerochem_vmr_* rows are the
! P_end (post-apply) capture the working vmr must reproduce bitwise -> ALL
! aerochem rows are kept as the primary gate (the keep rule also shields
! aerochem_vmr_num_a2 from the num_a2 glob below). The after tape's
! aerochem_vmr_postnewnuc/postcoag rows produce no check rows here: this
! suite never updates the checkpoint variables.
! The after tape's bare constituent rows hold the same post-apply state the
! suite's difference unpack lands on, but by a different arithmetic path:
! CAM's tape converts the applied sum fl((vmr+d*dt)*a) while the unpack
! applies the converted tendency fl(vmr*a)+fl(dt*fl(d*a)), so every species
! gasaerexch/rename touch keeps the documented ~1-2 ulp apply-space relative
! floor (see HANDOFF.md) -> absorbed by min_difference, rows still checked.
! The floor is amplified above min_difference only where rename's
! aitken->accum merge removes most of the aitken number: num_a2 (~1.4e-9
! relative) and num_c2 (~7.4e-10) -> excluded (leading wildcard also covers
! a possible cnst_ label prefix).
! Still hard-checked: all aerochem_vmr_* rows (bitwise), the recovered
! del_h2so4_aeruptk vs the after tape's capture (bitwise, via mam_vmr_apply),
! untouched species, and all other touched constituents within
! min_difference.
ncdata_check_exclude = '!aerochem_vmr_*', '*num_a2', '*num_c2'
ncdata_check_err = .true.
min_difference = 2e-15

